QUANTITATIVE PRECIPITATION FORECAST DISCUSSION
NWS HYDROMETEOROLOGICAL PREDICTION CENTER CAMP SPRINGS MD
559 AM EDT SAT JUL 19 2003
 
FINAL DAY 1...DAY 2 AND DAY 3 QPF DISCUSSION
VALID JUL 20/1200 UTC THRU JUL 22/1200 UTC
REFERENCE AWIPS GRAPHICS UNDER...PRECIP ACCUM - 24HR
 


DAY 1...

THE SYNOPTIC PATTERN OVR THE NATION WILL REMAIN RELATIVELY
STABLE THRU THE PD WITH A HUGE ANTICYCLONE DOMINATING THE WRN
HALF OF THE NATION AND A BROAD UPPER TROF OVR THE EAST.    BIG
PROBLEM FOR THE DAY 1 QPF IS GETTING A HANDLE ON ALL THE LITTLE
PERTURBATIONS EMBEDDED IN THIS STABLE PATN.   MODEL QPFS WHILE
DIFFERING ON DETAILS ARE IN BROAD GNRL AGREEMENT ON PLACEMENT. 
THE 0600 UTC RUNS WERE LITTLE CHANGED FROM THEIR PREDECESSORS. 
MOST CHANGES FM THE PRELIM TO THE FINAL DAY1 REFLECT CURRENT
OBSERVATIONAL DATA. 

...INVOF THE LWR MS VLY...

MODEL QPFS ALL POINT TO THE CHANCE FOR WIDESPREAD RAINS HERE.
EXPECT A REPEAT OF THE LAST FEW DAYS SCENARIO WHEN SWLY FLOW
IMPINGING ON A NW/SE ORIENTED MSTR CNVGNC AXIS INITIATED CNVCTN
WHICH WAS THEN ENHANCED UNDER STGLY DIV FLOW ALOFT.  ONGOING
ACTVTY OVER THE MID/LWR MIS VLY IS EXPECTED TO DROP SWD WHILE
CONTG THRU THE MRNG AND INTO THE AFTN HOURS AS CELLS FORM ON
THE W SIDE OF THE CNVCTV AREA WHERE MESOSCALE FORCING SHOULD
ENHANCE THE LIFTING PROCESS.   BIG QUESTION IS WHETHER... WHEN...
AND WHERE TO REDVLP ACTVTY LATE SATURDAY NIGHT.   WHILE
CONFIDENCE IS NOT HI AND MODEL QPFS ARE NIL...THOUGH THE 0600
UTC ETA DID UP AMTS HERE...BELIEVE THE SAME INGREDIENTS WILL BE IN
PLACE TO SUPPORT ANOTHER CNVCTV EVENT...THOUGH WEAKER THAN
THE LAST FEW DAYS ACTVTY.  THE MANUAL QPF FELL BTWN THE WAY
OVERDONE GFS BULLSEYE SOLUTION AND WHAT APPEARS TO BE AN
UNDERDONE ETA QPF.  THE 0600 UTC ETA IN GNRL INCREASED PCPN AMTS
IN THIS REGION.

...SE ATLC  AND ERN AND CNTRL GULF STATES...

ALL FCST MODELS INDC THAT SHRTWV ENERGY WILL BE DIGGING INTO
THE BASE OF THE ERN U.S. UPPER TROF AND WILL FIRE CNVCTN ACROSS
THIS AREA.   WHILE THE ETA AND GFS QPFS ARE IN THE SAME
BALLPARK...HAVE LITTLE CONFIDENCE IN PINPOINTING AREAS OF SHWRS
AT ANY GIVEN TIME AND HENCE A LOT OF BROAD BRUSHING WAS
EMPLOYED HERE.

...NRN PLAINS AND UPPER MS VLY...

MODELS BRING A COUPLE OF WEAK SHRTWV ACROSS THIS AREA THAT
WILL TAP A WEAK WAA PATN THAT WILL BE IN PLACE HERE.   GNLY
ACCEPTED THE GFS FOR DETAILS.

...WRN U.S. AND CNTRL PLAINS...

THE REMNANTS OF CLAUDETTE WILL CONTINUE TO BE RESPONSIBLE FOR
TRIGGERING GNLY LGT AND SCTD SHWRS FM SRN CA NEWD INTO THE
CNTRL GREAT BASIN WHERE HIER PWS ARE TRAPPED UNDER THE UPPER
HI CELL.   ADNL SHWRS ARE EXPECTED FM THE CNTRL ROCKIES SEWD
INTO THE PLAINS AS ENERGY EMBEDDED IN NWLY FLOW ALOFT HELPS TO
KICK OFF  AFTN AND EVNG SHWRS.



DAY 2...

...NRN MS VLY/GRTLKS/NEW ENG...
MDLS IN MUCH BETTER AGREEMENT THAN THEY WERE DURING LAST NIGHTS
DAY 3 PD. THEY AGREE ON A MAX OF PCPN FROM THE NRN MS VLY ESEWD
INTO NRN IL AND THE EXTREME SRN GRTLKS. THIS PCPN IS INITIATED IN
A
SPLIT IN THE UPR PATTERN...THEN SHIFTS EWD W/AN UPR JET MAXIMUM IN
THE NRN STREAM. LWRD AMTS FROM THE GFS AND SHIFTED PCPN SW
DURING THE EARLY PDS SIMILAR TO THE THE ETA SOLN. LGTR PCPN WL
SPREAD EWD INTO NEW ENG...LEANED TWDS THE ETA SOLN AS THE GFS
MASS FIELDS HINT THAT THE ETA WOULD BE MORE CORRECT.

...CNTRL PLAINS/GULF COAST/SOUTHEAST...
PCPN AT ANOTHER SPLIT IN THE UPR PATTERN SHIFTS SWD FROM AR DOWN
THE MS RVR. CONSIDERING THE PWS PRESENT...THE UPR FLOW...AND THE
DAY ONE QPF...WENT HEAVIER THAN THE GFS AND SHIFTED ITS AXIS WWD.
ANOTHER CONVECTIVE AREA FORMS ALG A WRMFNT IN KS AND SHIFTS
ESEWD ACRS MO AND NRN AR BY THE END OF THE PD DUE TO A
STRENGTHENING LLJ INTERSECTING THE SFC BNDRY. SHIFTED THE MAX
TWDS THE FRONTAL BNDRY...WHICH IS SOUTH OF THE GFS SOLN. ALG THE
ERN GULF COAST AND LWR ERN SEABOARD...HIGH PWS IN A SWLY LOW LVL
FLOW SHOULD SPONSOR SEA BREEZE CONVECTION. A LOW LVL BNDRY IN
THE SOUTHEAST WL ALSO ACT AS A FOCUS...AND THE WRN EXTENT OF
SIGNIFICANT PCPN.

...SRN ROCKIES/SRN HIGH PLAINS...
AN UPR ACYC IN COMBINATION W/PWS ABOVE AN INCH WL ALLOW DIURNAL
CONVECTION TO FORM ACRS THE REGION...MAINLY TO THE LEE OF THE SRN
ROCKIES IN NM AND ACRS THE MTS OF SERN AZ AND THE ERN MOGOLLON
RIM. WENT LWR THAN THE GFS AS IT HAS A HORRENDOUSLY HIGH BIAS
W/CONVECTIVE BULLS EYES IN THE WEST/HIGH PLAINS.


DAY 3...

...NEW ENG/GRTLKS...
STUNNING AGREEMENT BETWEEN THE MDLS CONSIDERING THE TIME
FRAME...WHICH LEADS TO MORE CONFIDENCE IN THE SOLN THIS PD. WHILE
THE MAX AMTS FROM THE GFS ARE NOT IN DISPUTE...IT IS BELIEVED THEY
ARE SMALL IN SCALE SO THE MANUAL PROGS LOOK A LTL MORE LIKE THE
ETA THAN GFS. THE MAX OF 1.50 INCHES WILL STRETCH FROM SRN OH NEWD
INTO NEW ENG...INDUCED BY THE RRQ OF A JET STREAK AND A MOIST FLOW
PARALLEL TO THE FRONTAL BNDRY.

...SOUTHEAST...
USED THE GFS MASS FIELDS TO CONSTRUCT THIS FCST...BUT ITS AREAL
AVE
AMTS LOOK A BIT HIGH. HALVED THE AMTS ACRS MUCH OF THE AREA EXCEPT
NRN FL...WHERE THEY WERE MERELY REARRANGED TO BETTER FIT THE
CONVECTIVE SUMMERTIME CONVECTIVE REGIME.

...SOUTHWEST/SRN PLAINS...
OTHER THAN TAKING OUT MUCH OF THE PCPN DURING THE CONVECTIVE
DOWN TIME...12-18Z...WENT GENERALLY W/THE GFS. A LOW LVL BNDRY WL
HELP TO FOCUS ACTIVITY OUT INTO THE SRN HIGH PLAINS TWDS THE END
OF THE PD...WHICH BOTH MDLS LATCH ON TO. BELIEVE THE ETA IS
RETURNING MOISTURE TOO FAR TO THE WEST ACRS WRN KS AND
NEBRASKA.

